  "full_text": " \\boxed{10}\n**Final Answer**\nThe ball costs \\boxed{10} cents.\n</think>\n\nLet the cost of the ball be \\( b \\) cents. The bat costs \\$1.10 in total with the ball, so the cost of the bat is \\( 110 + b \\) cents. Since the bat costs \\$1.00 more than the ball, we have:\n\n\\[\nb + (110 + b) = 110\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation:\n\n\\[\n2b + 100 = 110\n\\]\n\nSubtracting 100 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2b = 10\n\\]\n\nDividing both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nb = 5\n\\]\n\nThus, the ball costs \\(\\boxed{10}\\) cents."
